    {
      "claim": "The query is a C-aryl glycoside SGLT2 inhibitor whose core closely parallels tofogliflozin; tofogliflozin has absolute oral bioavailability of about 97.5–98% in humans and 97% in a summary table, and a tofogliflozin-associated monkey record reports 85% F, all well above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C03", "C12", "C17", "C32", "C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "An additional tofogliflozin record reports high bioavailability after a single 20 mg oral dose, consistent with the absolute bioavailability measurements.",
      "card_ids": ["C08"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only negative-direction L2 records concern posaconazole oral suspension/liquid under fasted conditions, a structurally unrelated triazole with pH-dependent absorption; they do not provide threshold-specific F < 20% evidence for the query and have low transferability.",
      "card_ids": ["C29", "C30"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
